@meta
  project: HMLR
  title: HyperMedia Language Runtime & Browser DevTools Extension
  version: 1.0.0
  runtime: hmlr@1.0
  repo: github.com/hyperlibs/HMLR
  license: MIT
  architecture: Common Language Runtime & WebExtension Suite

@type PanelType = signals* | audit | spatial | diagnostics
@type TargetEngine = htmxui* | htmfx | hmlr_wasm | legacy_js
@type Severity = info* | warning | error | critical

@model ExtensionPanel
  id: string
  title: string
  panel_type: PanelType
  target: TargetEngine
  active: bool

@model AuditMetric
  name: string
  score_pct: int
  payload_kb: float
  swap_latency_ms: float
  token_cost_llm: int
  purity_grade: string

# HMLR: HyperMedia Language Runtime & DevTools Inspector
A high-performance Common Language Runtime (CLR-style) virtual machine (<50KB Wasm) paired with a Chromium/Firefox DevTools extension (.crx).
Replaces generic Lighthouse auditing with hypermedia velocity metrics, inspects live HxBolt signal graphs, tracks htmFX 3D spatial viewports, and streams token-dense .mx diagnostics for autonomous AI self-healing.

## Extension DevTools Panels | @model ExtensionPanel
| id           | title                        | panel_type   | target       | active |
| panel-signals| ⚡ Reactive Signal Graph      | signals      | htmxui       | true   |
| panel-audit  | 🚀 Hypermedia Velocity Audit | audit        | htmxui       | true   |
| panel-spatial| 🪐 3D Spatial & Physics HUD  | spatial      | htmfx        | true   |
| panel-diag   | 🤖 Agentic .mx Telemetry     | diagnostics  | hmlr_wasm    | true   |

## Hypermedia Audit vs. Chrome Lighthouse | @model AuditMetric
| name                  | score_pct | payload_kb | swap_latency_ms | token_cost_llm | purity_grade |
| Pure Hypermedia Flow  |       100 |       1.40 |            0.80 |             95 | AAA (Zero JS)|
| Reactive Signal Patch |        98 |       0.20 |            0.15 |             28 | AAA          |
| 3D Spatial Viewport   |        96 |      17.60 |            1.20 |             80 | AA+ (WebGPU) |
| Legacy React/JSON SPA |        42 |     480.00 |           45.00 |           1850 | D- (Heavy JS)|

## Architecture of HMLR DevTools Extension

```text
extension/
├── manifest.json              # WebExtension Manifest V3 (Chrome, Edge, Firefox)
├── background.ts              # Service worker auto-detecting htmx, htmxUI & htmFX
├── content_script.ts          # Zero-overhead bridge inspecting DOM, signals, and viewports
└── devtools/
    ├── devtools.html          # DevTools Tab Container
    ├── panel_signals.mx       # Panel A: Real-time HxBolt signal graph & time-travel replay
    ├── panel_audit.mx         # Panel B: Hypermedia Velocity audit engine (Lighthouse bypass)
    ├── panel_spatial.mx       # Panel C: htmFX 3D entity coordinate tracker & fog inspector
    └── panel_agentic.mx       # Panel D: Live @diag FX-XXXX streaming telemetry
```

## Manifest V3 Specification (`extension/manifest.json`)

```json
{
  "manifest_version": 3,
  "name": "HMLR — HyperMedia Language Runtime & Spatial DevTools",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Native DevTools inspector and velocity auditor for htmxUI, htmFX, and .mx/.fx runtimes.",
  "devtools_page": "devtools/devtools.html",
  "background": {
    "service_worker": "background.js"
  },
  "content_scripts": [
    {
      "matches": ["<all_urls>"],
      "js": ["content_script.js"],
      "run_at": "document_start"
    }
  ],
  "permissions": ["activeTab", "storage"]
}
```

## Flat .mx Spatial DevTools Panel Layout (`panel_signals.mx`)

```mx
@viewport 1280x720

# Panel Header
@pin[top-left]:         Header("⚡ HxBolt Signal Tree", sub: "Active Reactive Scopes")
@pin[top-right]:        TelemetryBadge("120 FPS Ticker Synchronized", color: "emerald")

# Main Inspection Viewport
@pin[left-sidebar]:     SignalTree(filter: searchSignal, select: activeSignalScope)
@pin[center]:           StateInspector(scope: activeSignalScope, timeTravel: true)
@pin[bottom-bar]:       ActionBar(
                          Button("⏪ Step Backward", action: $timeTravel(-1)),
                          Button("⏩ Step Forward", action: $timeTravel(1)),
                          Button("📋 Copy State as .mx", action: $copyStateMatrix())
                        )
```

## Autonomous AI Healing & Streaming Diagnostics (`panel_agentic.mx`)

```mx
@diag FX-04012: UnresolvedRouteTarget
  file: routes/dashboard.mx:14:8
  cause: Typo in route target '/analyticss'
  candidates: /analytics | /settings
  fix: /analytics

@diag FX-01089: UnusedSignalScope
  file: views/cockpit.mx:22:1
  cause: Signal 'isMuted' declared in hx-state but never bound in child nodes
  fix: Bind with hx-text or remove from state object
```

## Runtime Kernel (.fx Implementation Blueprint)

```fsharp
// runtime/src/diagnostics_stream.fx
module HMLR.Diagnostics

type DiagnosticCode = string
type Severity = Error | Warning | Info

type DiagnosticEntry = {
    Code: DiagnosticCode
    Severity: Severity
    FilePos: string
    Culprit: string
    FixSuggestion: string
}

let formatDiagnosticMx (entry: DiagnosticEntry) : string =
    $"@diag {entry.Code}: {entry.Severity}\n  file: {entry.FilePos}\n  culprit: {entry.Culprit}\n  fix: {entry.FixSuggestion}\n"
```

## Exported Runtime Targets
- Browser DevTools Extension: `dist/hmlr-devtools.crx` & `dist/hmlr-devtools.zip`
- Edge Execution VM: `dist/hmlr.wasm` (<50KB) with Cloudflare Worker `fetch(req) -> Response` entry point.
- Host Integration Bridge: Attaches seamlessly to `window.HMLR` when present in the DOM.
